@startuml

title One import: the XML is read once, and only rows cross the component boundary

actor "Report author" as author
participant "ores.ore\nrun_configuration_handler" as handler
participant "ores.ore\nrun_configuration_operations" as ops
participant "projection\nread / map" as proj
queue "NATS" as bus
participant "ores.refdata\nconfiguration_document_handler" as h
participant "curve_configuration\n_document_service" as svc
participant "entity mapper" as mapper
database "ores_refdata_*_configs_tbl" as db

author -> handler : import a report's ORE input
handler -> handler : start a workflow, answer at once
handler -> ops : import_run(report definition, the files)
ops -> proj : read(curveconfig.xml)
proj --> ops : typed document, renderings as written
ops -> proj : map(document)
proj --> ops : rows
ops -> bus : save_curve_configuration_document_request
bus -> h : authorise refdata::curve_configurations:write
h -> svc : save(document)
svc -> mapper : domain row to entity
mapper -> mapper : rendering to stored form
mapper -> db : insert
db --> svc : accepted, or the value set's name in the error

note over proj
  Nothing in ores.ore knows a table, and
  nothing in refdata knows an element.
end note

@enduml
